---
// Credit assignment through time, shown at DECISION NODES: each node is a
// position with probability bars over the legal options and one option
// actually played. The terminal +1 flows backward up the spine, stamps each
// node, and the update happens per-node: the played bar grows, rivals shrink.
type Opt = { label: string; w: number; w2: number; picked?: boolean };
type Node = { tag: string; bad?: boolean; opts: Opt[] };

const NODES: Node[] = [
	{
		tag: 'decision 14 · hand: 1 cloth',
		opts: [
			{ label: 'take a good', w: 41, w2: 45, picked: true },
			{ label: 'take camels', w: 34, w2: 32 },
			{ label: 'sell a set', w: 25, w2: 23 },
		],
	},
	{
		tag: 'decision 121 · holding a diamond',
		bad: true,
		opts: [
			{ label: 'trade the diamond away', w: 9, w2: 12, picked: true },
			{ label: 'take a good', w: 55, w2: 53 },
			{ label: 'take camels', w: 36, w2: 35 },
		],
	},
	{
		tag: 'decision 268 · hand: 3 cloth',
		opts: [
			{ label: 'sell the set', w: 33, w2: 37, picked: true },
			{ label: 'take a good', w: 42, w2: 40 },
			{ label: 'take camels', w: 25, w2: 23 },
		],
	},
];
---

<figure class="crd">
	<div class="nodes">
		{NODES.map((n, i) => (
			<>
				{i > 0 && <div class="dots" aria-hidden="true">⋮</div>}
				<div class={`node${n.bad ? ' bad' : ''}`}>
					<span class="tag">{n.tag}</span>
					<span class="opts">
						{n.opts.map((o) => (
							<span class={`opt${o.picked ? ' picked' : ''}`}>
								<span class="olbl">{o.picked ? '► ' : ''}{o.label}</span>
								<span class="track"><span class="fill" style={`--w:${o.w}%;--w2:${o.w2}%`}></span></span>
								<span class="pct">{o.w}%</span>
								<span class={`delta ${o.picked ? 'up' : 'dn'}`}>{o.picked ? '▲' : '▼'}</span>
							</span>
						))}
					</span>
					<span class="stamp w">+1</span>
				</div>
			</>
		))}
		<div class="dots" aria-hidden="true">⋮</div>
		<div class="outcome win">WIN +1</div>
	</div>

	<div class="others">
		<div class="mrow">
			another game · hand: 3 gold · <em>sold the set</em>
			<span class="pill w">won +1</span>
		</div>
		<div class="mrow">
			another game · hand: 3 spice · <em>sold the set</em>
			<span class="pill l">lost −1</span>
		</div>
		<div class="tally">
			selling a matched set <em>from positions like these</em>:
			<span class="pill w">+1</span><span class="pill w">+1</span><span class="pill l">−1</span>
			<span class="verdict">the vote leans yes</span>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="crd-controls">
		<button class="crd-back" type="button">← Back</button>
		<span class="crd-count"></span>
		<button class="crd-next" type="button">Next →</button>
	</div>

	<figcaption class="crd-caption" aria-live="polite"></figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.crd {
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
		padding: 1.2rem 1.2rem 1rem;
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 14px;
	}
	.nodes {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: stretch;
		gap: 0.15rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
	}
	.dots {
		text-align: center;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		line-height: 1;
	}
	.node {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 172px 1fr 44px;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.6em;
		padding: 0.4em 0.6em;
		border: 1.5px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 9px;
		transition: border-color 0.3s ease, background 0.3s ease;
	}
	.crd.s3 .node.bad {
		border-color: #b4341f;
		background: #faf1ee;
	}
	.tag {
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		line-height: 1.3;
	}
	.opts {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.18rem;
	}
	.opt {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 128px 1fr 34px 14px;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.4em;
	}
	.olbl {
		font-size: 0.66rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		text-align: right;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}
	.opt.picked .olbl {
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
	}
	.track {
		position: relative;
		height: 9px;
		background: rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 3px;
	}
	.fill {
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0 auto 0 0;
		width: var(--w);
		background: #c3c9d4;
		border-radius: 3px;
		transition: width 0.5s ease;
	}
	.opt.picked .fill {
		background: var(--accent);
	}
	.crd.s4 .fill {
		width: var(--w2);
	}
	.pct {
		font-size: 0.64rem;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
	}
	.delta {
		font-size: 0.6rem;
		opacity: 0;
		transition: opacity 0.35s ease;
	}
	.delta.up {
		color: #177a4c;
	}
	.delta.dn {
		color: #b4341f;
	}
	.crd.s4 .delta {
		opacity: 1;
	}
	.stamp {
		justify-self: center;
		padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
		border-radius: 999px;
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		opacity: 0;
		transition: opacity 0.45s ease;
	}
	.stamp.w {
		background: #eaf4ee;
		border: 1.5px solid #177a4c;
		color: #177a4c;
	}
	.crd.s2 .stamp {
		opacity: 1;
	}
	.outcome {
		align-self: center;
		padding: 0.3em 0.8em;
		border-radius: 8px;
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.outcome.win {
		border: 1.5px solid #177a4c;
		background: #eaf4ee;
		color: #177a4c;
	}
	.others {
		visibility: hidden;
		opacity: 0;
		transition: opacity 0.4s ease;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.3rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
	}
	.crd.s5 .others {
		visibility: visible;
		opacity: 1;
	}
	.mrow,
	.tally {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 0.35rem;
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
	}
	.mrow em,
	.tally em {
		font-style: normal;
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.pill {
		padding: 0.05em 0.4em;
		border-radius: 999px;
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 0.72rem;
	}
	.pill.w {
		background: #eaf4ee;
		border: 1.5px solid #177a4c;
		color: #177a4c;
	}
	.pill.l {
		background: #faf1ee;
		border: 1.5px solid #b4341f;
		color: #b4341f;
	}
	.verdict {
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
	}
	.crd-controls {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-top: 0.9rem;
		padding-top: 0.6rem;
		border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}
	.crd-controls button {
		font: inherit;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		padding: 0.35em 1em;
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: #fff;
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.crd-controls button:hover:not(:disabled) {
		border-color: var(--accent);
		color: var(--accent);
	}
	.crd-controls button:disabled {
		opacity: 0.35;
		cursor: default;
	}
	.crd-count {
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		min-width: 3.5em;
		text-align: center;
	}
	.crd-caption {
		min-height: 9em;
		margin-top: 0.6rem;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
	}
	@media (max-width: 560px) {
		.node {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 2.6em;
		}
		.tag {
			grid-column: 1 / -1;
		}
	}
</style>

<script>
	type Step = { caption: string; cls: string[] };

	const STEPS: Step[] = [
		{
			caption:
				"Three of one game's roughly three hundred decisions. At each node the network read the position and spread its confidence across the legal options; the arrow marks the one it actually played. Each node is written into a ledger (the position, the options, the probabilities) and sits there unscored, because during play nothing comes back. The one number arrives at the end: +1 if the game is won, −1 if it is lost.",
			cls: [],
		},
		{
			caption:
				'This game was won, so a +1 flows backward through every node on the path, and each ledger row inherits it. That is the whole mechanism: the final result is the only credit there is, and every decision that led to it gets stamped with it.',
			cls: ['s2'],
		},
		{
			caption:
				'Look at the middle node. Trading the diamond away was a 9% long-shot; during training the network samples from its leanings rather than always playing the favourite, so long-shots get tried. This one collected a +1 because the game around it happened to be won. The stamp is blind. Blunders in wins get rewarded, brilliancies in losses get punished.',
			cls: ['s2', 's3'],
		},
		{
			caption:
				'Now the update, node by node: the bar of the played move grows a little and its rivals give up the difference. No bar is stored anywhere to edit; the only thing that changes is the 24,000 dials, each nudged (the dial-turning from Part 1, steered by the stamps) so that the played move scores a bit higher from that position. Nothing global happens to an action as an idea; three separate leanings shifted at three separate positions. A −1 would have pushed the same bars the other way.',
			cls: ['s2', 's4'],
		},
		{
			caption:
				'The rescue is volume, pooled by resemblance. Other games hold no identical position, but plenty of similar ones. The network cannot file each position separately; look-alikes lean on the same dials, so their nudges pull together: +1, +1, −1 for selling a matched set. Over thousands of games, moves that are genuinely good in a kind of position win the vote.',
			cls: ['s2', 's4', 's5'],
		},
	];

	document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.crd').forEach((root) => {
		const back = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.crd-back')!;
		const next = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.crd-next')!;
		const count = root.querySelector('.crd-count')!;
		const caption = root.querySelector('.crd-caption')!;
		let i = 0;

		const render = () => {
			const s = STEPS[i];
			root.classList.remove('s2', 's3', 's4', 's5');
			s.cls.forEach((c) => root.classList.add(c));
			caption.textContent = s.caption;
			count.textContent = `${i + 1} / ${STEPS.length}`;
			back.disabled = i === 0;
			next.disabled = i === STEPS.length - 1;
		};

		back.addEventListener('click', () => {
			if (i > 0) i -= 1;
			render();
		});
		next.addEventListener('click', () => {
			if (i < STEPS.length - 1) i += 1;
			render();
		});
		render();
	});
</script>
